# Repo-root fallback .gitignore. client/ and server/server/ already have their own, more specific
# .gitignore files (dist/dist-ssr, logs, etc.) — this one exists for anything created at the repo
# root itself (root-level .env, an accidental root node_modules/build) and for mobile/, which has
# its own Flutter-specific .gitignore (mobile/.gitignore) but still benefits from these generic
# entries applying repo-wide.

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.env
.env.*.local
*.log
.DS_Store
server/server/uploads/
server/server/server-log.txt
.vitest/

# Flutter (mobile/) — see mobile/.gitignore for the full Flutter-specific set; these are the
# generic patterns worth having apply at the repo root too.
mobile/.dart_tool/
mobile/build/
mobile/android/**/build

# Android release-signing secrets (production-readiness pass, Sept 2026) — NEVER commit a real
# signing keystore or its passwords. mobile/android/key.properties + upload-keystore.jks are
# generated once per app and must be backed up securely OUTSIDE git, not pushed to GitHub.
mobile/android/key.properties
mobile/android/*.jks
mobile/android/*.keystore

coverage/

# Local-machine artifacts, not project source (Claude Code settings, scratch outputs, files
# staged for manual deletion) — none of these belong in the repo history.
.claude/
Claude outputs/
_to_delete/
